# 🏗️ Architecture Enforcement

## Feature-Based Structure

- NEVER place components outside the feature they belong to
- ALWAYS use the feature directory structure: `src/features/[name]/components/`, `types/`, `validation/`
- MUST include `index.ts` barrel exports only for directories with multiple exports
- FORBIDDEN: `index.ts` files for single-component directories
- Screen components MUST end with `Screen` suffix

## Design System First

- FORBIDDEN: Direct React Native component usage in features (`View`, `Text`, `TouchableOpacity`, etc.)
- REQUIRED: Import all UI components from `@design-system/ui`
- REQUIRED: Use theme-based styling with `createStyles(theme)` pattern
- MUST use design tokens: `theme.spacing.md`, `theme.colors.text.primary`

## Absolute Imports Only

- REQUIRED: Use TypeScript path aliases (`@design-system`, `@features`, etc.)
- FORBIDDEN: Relative imports across feature boundaries
- MUST follow import order: React → Third-party → Internal (`@paths`) → Relative

## File Organization & Export Strategy

```
✅ CORRECT Structure:
src/features/[feature]/
├── components/
│   ├── ComponentA/
│   │   ├── ComponentA.tsx
│   │   └── ComponentA.styles.ts
│   ├── ComponentB/
│   │   ├── ComponentB.tsx
│   │   └── ComponentB.styles.ts
│   └── index.ts             # ✅ Barrel export for multiple components
├── [Feature]Screen.tsx
├── types/
│   ├── User.ts
│   ├── API.ts
│   └── index.ts             # ✅ Barrel export for multiple types
├── validation/
│   ├── rules.ts
│   ├── schemas.ts
│   └── index.ts             # ✅ Barrel export for multiple files
└── index.ts                 # ✅ Main feature export

✅ DESIGN SYSTEM - Grouped Components:
src/design-system/ui/
├── Input/
│   ├── Input/
│   │   ├── Input.tsx        # NO index.ts (single component)
│   │   └── Input.styles.ts
│   ├── FormField/
│   │   ├── FormField.tsx    # NO index.ts (single component)
│   │   └── FormField.styles.ts
│   └── index.ts             # ✅ Main group export
├── Button/
│   ├── Button.tsx
│   ├── BackButton.tsx
│   ├── Button.styles.ts
│   └── index.ts             # ✅ Exports multiple button components

❌ FORBIDDEN:
- Components scattered across random directories
- index.ts files for single-component directories
- Mixing feature logic in shared directories
```

## Export Rules

- **NO** `index.ts` for single-component directories
- **YES** `index.ts` for directories with multiple exports
- **Import directly**: `from './ComponentName/ComponentName'`
- **Use barrel exports**: for directories with multiple related files

## Naming Conventions

- Screen components: `[Feature]Screen.tsx`
- Component props: `[Component]Props`
- Style functions: `create[Component]Styles`
- Constants: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE`
- Files: `PascalCase.tsx` for components, `camelCase.ts` for utilities

## Import Standards

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT order:
import React from "react";
import { View } from "react-native";
import { useNavigation } from "@react-navigation/native";
import { Button, Text } from "@design-system/ui";
import { useTheme } from "@design-system/hooks";
import { Theme } from "@design-system/types"; // Regular import (preferred)
import { createStyles } from "./Component.styles";

// ❌ FORBIDDEN: Mixed import order or relative cross-feature imports
// ❌ FORBIDDEN: import type for Theme (use regular import for consistency)
```

## Import Type Rules

- **FORBIDDEN**: `import type { Theme }` — use regular `import { Theme }`
- **REQUIRED**: Regular imports for all design system types (consistency with 119 existing files)
- **PATTERN**: Only use `import type` for truly exceptional type-only imports if needed

## Component Structure Pattern

```typescript
// REQUIRED pattern for all components
export interface ComponentNameProps {
  // Explicit prop types — no optional catch-alls
}

export const ComponentName = ({ prop1, prop2 }: ComponentNameProps) => {
  const { theme } = useTheme(); // REQUIRED for styling
  const styles = createComponentStyles(theme); // REQUIRED pattern

  return (
    // Implementation using design system components only
  );
};
```

## Inline Functions in Render Paths

- FORBIDDEN: Anonymous inline functions in render paths (new reference every render)
- REQUIRED: Extract callbacks to named `useCallback`-wrapped handlers inside lists
- PREFERRED: Extract `renderItem` for `FlatList` to a named component outside the parent

## Asset Organization

```
src/assets/
├── icons/[context]/      # Icons grouped by usage context
├── images/[context]/     # Images grouped by feature
└── lottie/              # Animation files
```

## Component Export Pattern

- **REQUIRED**: Use named exports — avoid default exports except for screen components
- **PATTERN**: Export component and its types from the same file

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Named exports
export interface DoctorCardProps { /* ... */ }
export const DoctorCard = ({ ... }: DoctorCardProps) => { /* ... */ };

// ❌ FORBIDDEN: Default export for non-screen components
export default DoctorCard;
```

## Constants & Configuration

- REQUIRED: Define all app constants in `src/constants/index.ts`
- MUST use `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` for all constant names
- FORBIDDEN: Magic numbers or string literals scattered across feature files

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: src/constants/index.ts
export const TOAST_CONFIG = {
  TOP_OFFSET: 60,
};
export const ANIMATION_DURATION_MS = 250;
```

## Logging Standards

- REQUIRED: Use the structured logger utility — never use `console.log` in production code
- MUST use appropriate log levels: `debug`, `info`, `warn`, `error`
- FORBIDDEN: `console.log`, `console.error`, or `console.warn` in committed code

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
import { logger } from '@utils';
logger.info('User signed in', { userId: user.id });
logger.error('API call failed', { endpoint, error });

// ❌ FORBIDDEN
console.log('user:', user);
```
